course: dictionary
lesson: 14388
title: Short words, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: OS is an abbreviation, a short form of longer words. Capital letters often mean it is short for something, and the same letters can mean different things. The words around it are its context, so read them to find out which meaning you need.
explain: «The OS on my tablet runs every app I open.» The clues are tablet and app. OS means operating system, the main program that runs a computer or phone.
explain: «We checked the OS map before our walk.» The clues are map and walk. This OS is Ordnance Survey, the national mapping agency of Great Britain, and its maps are detailed and used for walking.
explain: «This hoodie is one size, so it is OS.» Clothes tell you OS means one size or oversized. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: OS is short for operating system: the main program that runs a computer or phone, such as Windows, macOS, Android or iOS.
fact: OS also stands for Ordnance Survey, the national mapping agency of Great Britain. «OS maps» are detailed maps used for walking.
fact: In Latin, «os» means bone (plural «ossa») or mouth (plural «ora»). In French, «os» means bone.
fact: In clothing, OS can mean one size or oversized.
fact: OS is not an English word on its own, so always check the context to find its meaning.
exercise: «The OS on my laptop runs every program I use.» What does OS mean here? | Ordnance Survey map | One size | Bone | *Operating system, the main program that runs a computer
exercise: «We used the OS map to find the path up the hill.» What does OS mean here? | Mouth | Operating system | One size | *Ordnance Survey, the national mapping agency of Great Britain
exercise: A label says «OS» on a hoodie. What might it mean? | Operating system | Ordnance Survey | *One size or oversized | Bone in Latin
test: «The OS on my tablet is old, so I need an update.» What does OS mean here? | Oversized | *Operating system | Bone | Ordnance Survey
test: In French, what does «os» mean? | Mouth | *Bone | Size | Map
exam: Why must you check the context before deciding what OS means? | Because you should always guess the first meaning you think of | Because OS is only ever a Latin word | *Because the same letters can mean operating system, Ordnance Survey, one size or bone, and the words around it show which one | Because OS always means the same thing
